-- title:
--   Finiteness of the supersingular places of X(Γ)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, let $p$ be a prime and suppose $K$ has characteristic $p$, and let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of finite index containing the translation matrix `ModularGroup.T`. Consider the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC K Γ` of reductions of ratios of integral $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma$. A place of this field over $K$ is, by the structure [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22), a valuation subring containing the image of $K$, different from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring. The theorem asserts that the set [`ModularCurve.ssPlacesQExp K Γ p`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L27) is finite, i.e. there are only finitely many places $v$ for which there are an element $x$ of the $q$-expansion function field whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) and an element $a \in K$ such that $x$ lies in the valuation ring of $v$ with residue the image of $a$ (the predicate `Place.HasValue`) and $a$ belongs to the set `ssJSet p K`.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the set of supersingular places on the curve $X(\Gamma)$ in characteristic $p$: those places at which the reduced $j$-invariant is regular and takes a value in `ssJSet p K`. It underlies the description of the special fibre of $X(\Gamma \cap \Gamma_0(p))$ at $p$, where the two components are glued at the supersingular points, and is used in the construction of models, differentials and Néron data for modular curves at $p$.
-- source:
